        "problem": "Find $|r(3)|$ given that $r(t)=\u27e82t-4,\\,\\sqrt{6t+7},\\,\\sqrt{t+4}\u27e9.$",
        "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =\u27e82(3)-4,\\,\\sqrt{6(3)+7},\\,\\sqrt{3+4}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82,\\,5,\\,\\sqrt{7}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(3)| & =\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(5)}^{2}+(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
